          "title": "You'll want to know: le carambolage",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le carambolage — \"the pile-up, the multiple crash\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Il y a eu un carambolage sur l'autoroute ce matin. There was a pile-up on the motorway this morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A billiards word first: caramboler is to hit two balls in one shot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "carambolage is built on caramboler \"to hit two balls at once\", from carambole, the red ball in billiards, which was borrowed from Spanish carambola (EtymDB lists the noun without a parent)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
