          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le chauffard — \"the reckless driver, the road hog\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Un chauffard a grillé le feu rouge. A reckless driver went through the red light."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The suffix -ard adds a scornful sense. Griller un feu — to run a red light."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chauffard is built on chauffeur \"driver\" with the scornful suffix -ard; chauffer \"to heat\" is inherited from Latin calefacere \"to make warm\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
